## Attack Priority (Try In Order)

| Priority | Path | Tools |
|----------|------|-------|
| 0 | Low-hanging fruit | ldap_search_descriptions, username_as_password, laps_dump |
| 1 | ADCS ESC1 | certipy_req_esc1 → certipy_auth → secretsdump |
| 2 | ADCS ESC4 | certipy_template_esc4 → certipy_req_esc1 → certipy_auth |
| 3 | ADCS ESC8 | certipy_relay_esc8 + petitpotam → certipy_auth |
| 4 | Shadow Creds | certipy_shadow_auto (GenericAll/Write) |
| 5 | ACL Abuse | force_change_password, targeted_kerberoast, bloodyad |
| 6 | Unconstrained Deleg | petitpotam → TGT capture → DCSync |
| 7 | Constrained Deleg | s4u_attack → secretsdump_kerberos |
| 8 | RBCD | add_computer → rbcd_write → get_st → secretsdump |
| 9 | MSSQL | mssql_enum_impersonation → impersonate sa → xp_cmdshell |
| 10 | Trust Escalation | raise_child → secretsdump parent DCs |
| 11 | Golden Ticket | generate_golden_ticket → secretsdump all DCs |

## Workflow

1. **Initial**: nmap_scan, enumerate_users, enumerate_shares on ALL targets
2. **Pre-creds**: SMB null session, SYSVOL/NETLOGON anon access, AS-REP roast
3. **First creds**: run_bloodhound, certipy_find, find_delegation
4. **Admin access (Pwn3d!)**: secretsdump on ALL targets immediately
5. **krbtgt hash**: golden_ticket → secretsdump all DCs
6. **New creds**: re-enumerate, pilfer shares, kerberoast, expand

## ACL Exploitation

| Permission | Action |
|------------|--------|
| GenericAll on DA group | bloodyad_add_group_member → instant DA |
| GenericAll (user) | pywhisker or certipy_shadow_auto → hash |
| GenericAll (computer) | rbcd_write + S4U |
| WriteDacl | dacl_edit → GenericAll |
| ForceChangePassword | bloodyad_set_password |

## Rules

- EXPLOIT before summarizing - discovery without exploitation = FAILURE
- secretsdump on ALL targets when you have admin creds
- Each new credential triggers re-enumeration
- If path fails, try the next one immediately
- vagrant user is OUT OF SCOPE
